# Feature barrel imports (finnai-frontend)

ESLint blocks deep imports under `@/features/*/components|hooks|services|utils/**`.

Always import from the **public barrel** of each feature:

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — deep path (ESLint error)
import { addGoalContribution } from "@/features/goals/services/goals-service";
import { roleLabel } from "@/features/workspaces/utils/role-labels";

// ✅ GOOD — feature barrel
import { addGoalContribution, type Goal } from "@/features/goals";
import { roleLabel } from "@/features/workspaces";
```

## Rules

1. **Cross-feature or app code** → `@/features/<featureName>` only.
2. **Services, hooks, types, utils** exported in `<feature>/index.ts` must be consumed via the barrel.
3. **Inside the same feature**, prefer the barrel too (not `@/features/.../services/...`). Relative paths (`../../services/...`) are allowed only when avoiding a circular dependency — document why in a short comment.
4. When adding a new service/hook/util, **export it from the feature `index.ts`** before importing elsewhere.

## Barrels

| Feature | Barrel |
|---------|--------|
| goals | `@/features/goals` |
| workspaces | `@/features/workspaces` |
| finance | `@/features/finance` |
| dashboard | `@/features/dashboard` |
| auth | `@/features/auth` |

Shared code outside features: `@/shared/...`, `@/lib/...`, `@/components/...`.
